  "title": "Al-Farabi",
  "summary": "Al-Farabi was a philosopher and music theorist, probably born in 870 CE at Farab (Farayb), who moved to Baghdad in his youth and later to Syria. He was called the second master after Aristotle, and his Great Book of Music is described as the most important medieval musical treatise in Islamic lands. He died in Damascus in December 950 or January 951.",
